WEBVTT

00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:19,920
I am currently trying vitamin C IVs and the ingredients are vitamin C, magnesium chloride, potassium chloride, calcium, agglucidate.

00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:24,920
Does that sound like a combination? Is there a reason why I should not do that?

00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:28,920
No, no. You can do that. That's just fine.

00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:42,920
They're always in vitamin C IV banks. There's other minerals and it has to do with keeping it in solution and keeping it aqueous for the ability for you to put it in your blood.

00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:53,920
So, you don't really have a choice with some of these other things. They're not put it in there for you to get magnesium, potassium, per se, but they're keeping it in the VH balance for your blood.

00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:57,920
So, that is just fine.

